  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a Phase 1 budget of $500,000 and a kick-off on June 15th. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. The team expanded by adding five members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding on September 10th. An R&D call for ideas regarding AI-enhanced data visualization was issued with a July 20th deadline. The project celebrated the completion of the testing phase on October 10th. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience was requested by the end of November. A recent update outlined next steps, including finalizing technical documentation, meeting with the steering committee, and preparing for a showcase event. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, were updated to take effect in January. Additionally, a $15,000 budget was approved for specialized training for the coding team and project managers, starting next month."
